<title>USA: Central U.S. carlot beef trade 1500 CST - USDA.</title>
<headline>Central U.S. carlot beef trade 1500 CST - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Utility carcass steady; Cutter steady to weak. Demand and offerings moderate. -USDA</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>    COW &amp; BULL CARCASS FOB OMAHA	 Six     Loads Reported.</p>
<p>			  Lds     Price Range    Latest Estb. Mkt.</p>
<p>UT,brk 2-4 450#/up  1.0   48.50		 48.50</p>
<p>UT,bng 1-3 400#/up  3.0   52.50		 52.50</p>
<p>Cutter 1-2 350#/up  2.0   55.00 - 56.00     55.00 - 56.00</p>
<p>Bulls YG 1 500#/up			    unq</p>
<p>BONELESS PROCESSING BEEF/BEEF TRIMMINGS 257.0 loads reported.</p>
<p>Fresh lean boneless beef 1.00-2.00 lower in the Midwest, but in Texas generally steady; 75% mostly steady; 65% 2.50-3.00 lower. Demand and offerings light to moderate. Beef trimmings generally lower on fairly good demand and heavy offerings.</p>
